  "question": "Student Management System Requirements Description:\nThis is a student management system. The main features of the system include:\n1. Student Information Management: Includes information such as name, gender, school, department, and major.\n2. Identification Information Management: Includes information such as identification number, name, gender, age, and address. Each student has unique identification information.",
  "ddl": "-- Schema for database: rschema_0141\nCREATE TABLE `student` (\n  `student_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `gender` varchar(10) NOT NULL,\n  `school` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `department` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `major` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`student_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `identification` (\n  `identification_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `student_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `id_number` varchar(50) NOT NULL,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `gender` varchar(10) NOT NULL,\n  `age` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `address` varchar(500) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`identification_id`),\n  UNIQUE KEY `student_id` (`student_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `identification_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`student_id`) REFERENCES `student` (`student_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;",
